[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Since \(m\) and \(n\) are coprime (i.e., \(\text{GCD}(m, n) = 1\)), the LCM of \(m\) and \(n\) is simply their product. Therefore, the LCM of \(a\) and \(b\) is:
