[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ 6 \text{ periods/day} \times 40 \text{ minutes/period} = 240 \text{ minutes/day} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Next, we need to calculate the total minutes he spends in class over the 5 days he goes to class each week:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ 240 \text{ minutes/day} \times 5 \text{ days/week} = 1200 \text{ minutes/week} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Now, let's calculate the total minutes he spends on extra learning time each week. He spends \( \frac{1}{16} \) of his weekly minutes on Saturday and Sunday:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ \frac{1}{16} \times 1200 \text{ minutes/week} = 75 \text{ minutes/week} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Finally, we add the minutes spent on class and the extra learning time to find the total minutes he spends learning each week:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
