[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Now, to find out how many cylindrical beakers are needed to fill the spherical tank, we divide the volume of the spherical tank by the volume of one cylindrical beaker:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ \text{Number of beakers} = \frac{V_{\text{sphere}}}{V_{\text{cylinder}}} = \frac{288 \pi}{72 \pi} = \frac{288}{72} = 4 \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
