[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 1. **Identify the properties of the isosceles triangle:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m    - Let the isosceles triangle have sides \(a\) and \(a\) (since it is isosceles), and the base \(b\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m    - The altitude from the vertex angle to the base divides the base into two equal segments of length \(b/2\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m    - The altitude also bisects the base into two equal segments of length \(b/2\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 2. **Determine the angles:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m    - Let the vertex angle be \(\theta\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m    - The base angles are each \(\frac{180^\circ - \theta}{2}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m    - The altitude from the vertex angle to the base forms two right triangles, each with a hypotenuse of length \(a\) and a leg of length \(a/2\). The angle between the altitude and the base is \(\theta\), so the other leg of the right triangle is \(a \cos \theta\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m    - The other leg of the right triangle is \(a \sin \theta\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m    - Therefore, we have the equation:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m      \[
