[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m [response] To find the volume of the cylindrical tube, we need to determine its radius and height. We are given the lateral surface area and the height of the cylinder. The formula for the lateral surface area of a cylinder is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
