[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m [response] To find the smallest possible value of the least common multiple (LCM) of \(a\) and \(b\), we start by noting the given conditions:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m - The units digit of \(a\) is 2.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m - The units digit of \(b\) is 4.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m - The greatest common divisor (GCD) of \(a\) and \(b\) is 6.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Since the GCD of \(a\) and \(b\) is 6, both \(a\) and \(b\) must be multiples of 6. Therefore, we can express \(a\) and \(b\) as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ a = 6m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ b = 6n \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m where \(m\) and \(n\) are integers.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
