[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Next, we need to find out how many sneakers were sold to the department store. Since the total number of sneakers is 48 and 17 were sold at the flash sale, the number of sneakers sold to the department store is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ 48 - 17 = 31 \text{ sneakers} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m The revenue from the department store is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ 31 \times 25 = 775 \text{ dollars} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Now, let's calculate the total revenue from both sales:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ 340 + 775 = 1115 \text{ dollars} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m The total cost of the sneakers is $576. Therefore, the profit is the total revenue minus the total cost:
