[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m [response] To determine the number of vertical asymptotes of the function \( y = \frac{2}{x^2 + x - 6} \), we need to identify the values of \( x \) that make the denominator zero, as these are the points where the function is undefined and potentially has vertical asymptotes.
