[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m First, recall the double-angle identity for sine:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \sin 2\theta = 2 \sin \theta \cos \theta
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m So, we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 2 \sin \theta \cos \theta = \frac{21}{25}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Dividing both sides by 2, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \sin \theta \cos \theta = \frac{21}{50}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Next, we need to find \(\cos \theta - \sin \theta\). Let's denote this expression by \(x\), so we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m x = \cos \theta - \sin \theta
