[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 2. **Use the fact that the altitudes intersect on the incircle:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m    The point where the altitudes intersect is the incenter of the triangle. The incenter is equidistant from all three sides of the triangle. The distance from the incenter to each side is the inradius \(r\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 3. **Relate the inradius to the sides of the triangle:**
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m    The inradius \(r\) of a triangle can be expressed as \(r = \frac{A}{s}\), where \(A\) is the area of the triangle and \(s\) is the semi-perimeter. The area \(A\) of the triangle can also be expressed as \(A = \frac{1}{2} \times a \times \sqrt{a^2 - \left(\frac{b}{2}\right)^2}\).
