[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m [response] To determine after how many seconds the two gears will next have both their marks pointing due north, we need to calculate the relative speeds of the two gears and then find the time it takes for their combined rotations to be equivalent to one full rotation (360 degrees).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m First, let's convert the first gear's rotation rate into degrees per second:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ 33 \frac{1}{3} = 33 + \frac{1}{3} = \frac{99}{3} + \frac{1}{3} = \frac{100}{3} \text{ degrees per second} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Next, let's convert the second gear's rotation rate into degrees per second:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ 45 \text{ rotations per minute} = 45 \times \frac{60}{60} = 45 \text{ degrees per second} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m The relative speed of the two gears is the difference in their rotation rates:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ \text{Relative speed} = \frac{100}{3} - 45 = \frac{100}{3} - \frac{135}{3} = -\frac{35}{3} \text{ degrees per second} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m The negative sign indicates that the second gear is moving in the opposite direction to the first gear. To find the time it takes for the two gears to align, we need to find the time it takes for the combined rotation to be equivalent to one full rotation (360 degrees):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ \text{Time} = \frac{360 \text{ degrees}}{\text{Relative speed}} = \frac{360}{\frac{35}{3}} = \frac{360 \times 3}{35} = \frac{1080}{35} \text{ seconds} \approx 30.23 \text{ seconds} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
