[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m    The orthocenter of the triangle is the point where the altitudes intersect, and the incenter is the point where the angle bisectors intersect. The orthocenter and the incenter are the same point in this case, so the triangle is isosceles with the vertex angle being \(120^\circ\).
