[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m [response] To find the speed of the particle, we need to determine the derivative of the position vector with respect to time \( t \). The position of the particle is given by the vector \(\left( 3 \sin \frac{t}{4}, 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \right)\). The speed \( v \) is the magnitude of the velocity vector, which is the derivative of the position vector with respect to \( t \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m The velocity vector is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \left( \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \sin \frac{t}{4} \right), \frac{d}{dt} \left( 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \right) \right) = \left( 3 \cos \frac{t}{4} \cdot \frac{1}{4}, -3 \sin \frac{t}{4} \cdot \frac{1}{4} \right) = \left( \frac{3}{4} \cos \frac{t}{4}, -\frac{3}{4} \sin \frac{t}{4} \right)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
