[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m First, we find the highest power of 3 that divides \( 15! \). This is given by the sum of the integer divisions of 15 by each of the powers of 3 from 1 to the largest integer \( k \) such that \( 3^k \leq 15 \).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \left\lfloor \frac{15}{3} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{15}{3^2} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{15}{3^3} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{15}{3^4} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{15}{3^5} \right\rfloor + \left\lfloor \frac{15}{3^6} \right\rfloor
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Calculating each term:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \left\lfloor \frac{15}{3} \right\rfloor = 5
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[
