[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m To find the volume of the pyramid, we first need to determine the area of the base and the height of the pyramid.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m The base of the pyramid is one face of the cube, which has a side length of 2. Therefore, the area of the base is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \text{Area of the base} = 2 \times 2 = 4
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m The apex of the pyramid is the center of the cube. The distance from the center of the cube to any of its vertices is half the length of the space diagonal of the cube. The space diagonal of a cube with side length \( s \) is given by \( s\sqrt{3} \). For a cube with side length 2, the space diagonal is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 2\sqrt{3}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Thus, the distance from the center to any vertex is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \frac{2\sqrt{3}}{2} = \sqrt{3}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m The height of the pyramid is the distance from the apex to the center of the base, which is \(\sqrt{3}\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m The volume \( V \) of a pyramid is given by the formula:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m V = \frac{1}{3} \times \text{Base Area} \times \text{Height}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Substituting the values we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m V = \frac{1}{3} \times 4 \times \sqrt{3} = \frac{4\sqrt{3}}{3}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Therefore, the volume of the pyramid is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[
