[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Since time cannot be negative, we take the absolute value:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ \text{Time} = 3 \text{ minutes} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Converting 3 minutes to seconds:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m \[ 3 \text{ minutes} \times 60 \text{ seconds per minute} = 180 \text{ seconds} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=26424)[0m Thus, the two gears will next have both their marks pointing due north after \boxed{180} seconds.
